<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johnny Briceño</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1960">1960</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as John Briceño</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johnny Briceño is a Belizean politician, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-united-party">People's United Party</a> and Prime Minister of Belize since November 2020. He had served as deputy prime minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-musa">Said Musa</a>. His party won the 2020 general election and was re-elected in 2025.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johnny-briceno.jpg" alt="Johnny Briceño" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Palácio do Planalto from Brasilia, Brasil · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johnny_Brice%C3%B1o_(52135383761)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
